        "original_id": "09f4554a-4a40-520c-9251-02e6863422d1",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Plants: Virgilia, Koeleria\n- Taxonomy: Fabaceae, grass family\n- Places: Southern Africa, Antarctica, oceanic islands\n\nFacts:\n- Virgilia is a genus of Southern African trees in the family Fabaceae.\n- Virgilia has shiny to hairy pinnate leaves, mauve to pink pea-shaped flowers, and leathery pods.\n- Koeleria is a common and widespread genus of plants in the grass family.\n- Koeleria is found on all continents except Antarctica and on various oceanic islands.",
